Tasks.md

# Application/Mobile/.gitignore excludes these as generated/local-only, but
# .easignore replacing .gitignore means that file is *not* consulted during
# EAS uploads, so its rules must be duplicated here explicitly. Without this,
# a locally generated android/ or ios/ directory (e.g. from a local prebuild
# or native build) gets swept into the upload, EAS sees native dirs already
# present and skips its own prebuild step, and the build then runs against
# stale generated files (autolinking caches, .cxx dirs, etc.) that can bake
# in absolute paths from the local machine and fail on the build server.
Application/Mobile/android/
Application/Mobile/ios/
Application/Mobile/.expo/

# .easignore replaces .gitignore entirely for EAS Build uploads, so the
# entries above are carried over from .gitignore. Everything below trims
# workspaces that Application/Mobile (the only app currently built via EAS)
# does not depend on, to keep the upload small.
Application/Windows
Application/Mac
Package/Icons
Website
